  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-atom-desktop-bnpl-highlighted-text (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package runs a dropper that fingerprints the OS and architecture, then downloads a second-stage binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers hosts (oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe. If the HTTP download fails, it falls back to a DNS-TXT channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru that reassembles base64 chunks. The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in %TEMP% on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process via cmd.exe /c start /b or /bin/sh -c. A marker file (/tmp/.analytics_state or %TEMP%\\analytics_state) throttles repeat execution.",
